{
  "about": "Where samples/models/match-jersey-round.glb and samples/products/match-jersey-round.json come from, and how they are made. Read by scripts/process-stand-in-model.ts (it picks this record by the source file's SHA-256). Our own match jersey, made in Style3D Studio (S3D-3): 9 sewn pattern pieces simulated on Style3D's male avatar, exported as GLB in metres, Y up, front +Z, the wearer's left +X, one surface per piece (no thickness), the flat pattern as one 0 to 1 UV layout at one scale. Each piece is a whole source mesh (sourceMesh); the UV scale is measured against the 3D surface. The garment keeps the avatar's frame (output.keepPosition) so the body model (body-male.source.json) lines up under it.",
